    {
      "id": "claim_9d7fde34b3e14747be88814d53a30bc7",
      "statement": "The observable behavior of an expired wait is 202 Accepted, not 408: the custom TimeoutException is never constructed anywhere in the code; ResultService.waitForResultHelper blocks on CompletableFuture.get(tlr.timeout.seconds, SECONDS), catches java.util.concurrent.TimeoutException, and returns Optional.empty(), which the controllers translate into the 202 + REQUEST_TIMED_OUT / REQUEST_TIMED_OUT_START_AND_WAIT responses; the GlobalExceptionHandler's 408 mapping for the custom TimeoutException is a defensive path for signatures that declare it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
